---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | Quantum ByTech"
  description="How Quantum ByTech collects, uses and protects the information you share through our website, by email and on WhatsApp, and how to ask us to change or delete it."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated October 30, 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--white">
    <div class="wrap legal-copy">
      <p>
        {site.name} ("we") is a digital studio in {site.location}. This page explains what information we collect, why,
        and what you can ask us to do with it. Questions: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Contact form:</strong> your name, company, email, phone or WhatsApp number, the services you tick, your message and the page you sent it from.</li>
        <li><strong>Messages you send us</strong> by email, WhatsApp or social media.</li>
        <li><strong>Client records</strong> when we work together: contact details, meetings, quotations, payments and project notes.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Our website does not use advertising or analytics cookies, and we do not track you across other sites.</p>

      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To reply to you, prepare quotations and schedule meetings.</li>
        <li>To deliver and support the work you hire us for, including invoices and payment reminders.</li>
        <li>To keep the business records we are required to keep.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We never sell your information or use it for advertising.</p>

      <h2>Services that process it for us</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts our internal admin panel and its database, and handles our email.</li>
        <li><strong>Formspree</strong> delivers contact-form messages to our inbox.</li>
        <li><strong>Resend</strong> sends emails from {site.email}, such as meeting invitations, quotations and reminders.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Calendar and Google Meet</strong> hold the meetings we book with you and their video links.</li>
        <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong> hosts this website.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Each of them only processes the information needed for that task.</p>

      <h2>Google account data</h2>
      <p>
        Our admin panel connects to Google Calendar only through our own company Google account, to create meetings and
        Google Meet links. We do not ask for or access the Google accounts of visitors or clients. Our use of
        information received from Google APIs follows the
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
        including the Limited Use requirements.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries that do not become projects are kept for up to two years. Client records are kept for as long as we
        work together and for as long as the law requires afterwards.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask us to show, correct or delete the information we hold about you, or to stop sending you reminders,
        by emailing <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. We reply within one working day.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        Our admin panel is private: every team member signs in with a password and an authenticator app, and the
        information is sent only over encrypted connections.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-hero { padding-block: clamp(56px, 8vw, 104px) clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px); }
  .updated { margin-top: 16px; color: var(--muted); }
  .legal-copy { max-width: 72ch; display: grid; gap: 16px; }
  .legal-copy h2 { font-size: var(--step-1); margin-top: 24px; }
  .legal-copy ul { display: grid; gap: 8px; padding-left: 1.2em; }
  .legal-copy a { color: var(--pine); font-weight: 600; }
</style>
